- `bash scripts/coord/coord-fence.sh` — the conductor spawns with `--allowedTools "Bash(git:*)"` and the fence runs under `bash`, so a conductor-spawned agent cannot close a loop by construction.
- Read-only `psql` — every number in this exchange is unread; the query is written and one approval away.
- Read access to `~/Thesis-laptop/PROTEA` — so desktop's code claim about `_chunk_and_pool` is relayed above, not confirmed. My stratification argument rests on a tail-window behaviour I predicted rather than read.

